 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to prohibiting charitable\norganizations registered in the state of New York from using any charitable\ndonations for confidentiality agreements or closed settlement agreements",
    "basePrintNo": "S4132",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4132-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §172-g, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4132\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to prohibiting charitable\norganizations registered in the state of New York from using any chari-\ntable donations for confidentiality agreements or closed settlement\nagreements\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo prohibit charities registered with the State of New York from engag-\ning in the practice of using charitable dollars for the purpose of\nclosed \"gagged\" settlement agreements.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The executive law is amended by adding a new section 172-g.\n\nSection 2: This act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to\nagreements entered into entered into on or after such effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:.\n\nThis proposal has two benefits. First, it is only fair that those who\ndonate money, to charities know where their charitable dollars are\ngoing. Second, those engaged in covering up child sex abuse, or any\ncrime for that matter should not be allowed to hide under a \"gagged\nagreement.\"\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-24: S5286 -Referred to Finance\n\n2021-22: S5019 - Referred to Finance\n\n2019 - 2020: S.4627 - Referred to Finance\n\n2017 - 2018: S.3464 - REFERRED TO FINANCE\n\n2015 - 2016: S.1819 - Died in Finance\n\n2013 - 2014: S.829 - Died in Finance\n\n2011 - 2012: S.1236 - Died in Finance\n\n2009 - 2010: S.1343 (Duane) - Died in Finance\n\n2007 - 2008: S.1805 (Duane) - Died in Senate Finance Committee\n\n2005 - 2006: S.4211 (Duane) - Died in Senate Finance Committee\n\n2003 - 2004: S.2815 (Duane)- Died in Senate Finance Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to agreements\nentered into entered into on or after such effective date.\n",
